WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.670
- How long have you known
each other though? You both?

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.960
- Since I was 17 years old.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.099
- Wait, 17?

00:00:06.099 --> 00:00:08.616
- And I was five, and
I was five back then.

00:00:08.616 --> 00:00:11.080
(audience laughs)

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.440
- No, wait, what's that story?

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.010
What do you mean 17 years old?

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:14.959
How did you meet?

00:00:14.959 --> 00:00:18.020
- Well, I used to teach
dance and cheerleading camps,

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.228
and where we were teaching a lot,

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:23.110
I thought about an idea
to give the winners

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:24.555
who would win in competitions

00:00:24.555 --> 00:00:27.140
the concerts that were in town,

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.360
and it just so happened to be Journey.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.710
And I got all these cheerleaders

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:34.300
who won prizes and awards
to come to the show

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.530
and I took them backstage,

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.060
and we were all in our cheer gear,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.210
and we met Randy as a bass player.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.188
- Oh, that's so crazy.

00:00:44.188 --> 00:00:45.021
(overlapping chatter)

00:00:45.021 --> 00:00:48.490
- And I was wearing crazy outfits, Carls.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:50.430
- You were wearing crazy outfits?

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.320
- Well, you had to at that time,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.867
you know how the dog does it.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.200
(audience laughs)

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.488
- Oh, I love you so much.

00:00:56.488 --> 00:00:58.660
Well, wait, Paula, there's something else

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.680
that I found interesting, I
did not know until yesterday,

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.902
did Michael Bolton sing
lullabies when he babysat you?

00:01:06.902 --> 00:01:08.518
- Yeah.

00:01:08.518 --> 00:01:10.040
(Randy laughs)

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.157
- Well, yes.

00:01:11.157 --> 00:01:14.310
I lived in a condominium,
and my oldest sister, Wendy,

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.930
was really good friends with Michael.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.150
And his name was Michael
Boloton, that was his name,

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:23.140
and he was an aspiring
singer-songwriter from Connecticut.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.800
And he used to come out in the summers

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.420
'cause he had his girlfriend,

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.036
who ended up being his
wife later on, Maureen,

00:01:29.036 --> 00:01:32.460
and we were all together, and
I would be in my brown uniform

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.010
and no one wanted to babysit.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.150
And we'd make Michael,

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.300
Michael would have to babysit,

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.530
but he was the worst babysitter

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.288
'cause all he cared about was music.

00:01:40.288 --> 00:01:41.121
(audience laughs)

00:01:41.121 --> 00:01:42.547
- That panned out though, didn't it?

00:01:42.547 --> 00:01:44.410
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.590
- And then Paula and I connected again

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.331
because when Perry left the
band, when Journey broke up,

00:01:49.331 --> 00:01:51.831
after the last two events
that I was on with them,

00:01:51.831 --> 00:01:53.790
we did a record with Michael Bolton;

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.440
we did "Sittin' On The Dock Of The Bay"

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.340
and "When A Man Loves A Woman",

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.220
and I was in LA, and Paula and I

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.380
hung out with Michael
Bolton and Irene Cara.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.200
God, Paula, we lived some life, yoh.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.700
- Ain't that crazy? How
different the chapters?

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.080
You look at your life and almost
like chapters, it's insane,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.554
like who comes in and out,
and who comes back around,

00:02:14.554 --> 00:02:16.093
it's a crazy thing.

